":0.4694038258323817,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":0.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.05034846766709792,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":37.1,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.010320975454301481,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":5.2,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.9993531618573146,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-1.0,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.1290903765895805,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.025552645732106027,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":37.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.32635486782114875,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":-0.003554287097831893,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":46.4,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03228916898031298,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":47.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.005454136102631013,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":43.2,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.007654162204300348,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":87.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.57692003,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"RPC, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages provision of a range of oilfield services and equipment for the oil and gas companies involved in the exploration, production, and development of oil and gas properties. The company operates through Technical Services and Support Services segments. The Technical Services segment offers pressure pumping, cementing, downhole tools, coiled tubing, snubbing, nitrogen, well control, wireline, and fishing services that are used in the completion, production, and maintenance of wells, as well as well control training. The Support Services segment provides a range of rental tools drill pipe and related tools, as well as pipe handling, pipe inspection and storage services. It rents its tools for use with onshore and offshore oil and gas well drilling, completion, and workover activities. It operates in Africa, Canada, Argentina, Mexico, Latin America, and the Middle East. The company was incorporated in 1984 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ben M. Palmer | CEO, President & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $562K ranks in the bottom quartile among Energy peers. Each employee generates $18K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["RPC, Inc. is a small-cap energy business with a $1.2B market cap on $1.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $53M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.28\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -11.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 15\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 58% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (41.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 145% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.7pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 34% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 29% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Among the least levered in Energy \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Don't Buy RPC, Inc. (NYSE:RES) For Its Next Dividend Without Doing These Checks","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-res/rpc/news/dont-buy-rpc-inc-nyseres-for-its-next-dividend-without-doing","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793976193.754,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"RPC, Inc. (RES): Is Its Net Cash Position Enough to Protect the Dividend?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/rpc-inc-res-net-cash-153936121.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793893176.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Can RPC (RES) Justify Its Valuation Following A Revenue Gain And Impairment Led Loss?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-res/rpc/news/can-rpc-res-justify-its-valuation-following-a-revenue-gain-a","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793881688.489,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What Makes RPC (RES) a New Buy Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3023272/what-makes-rpc-res-a-new-buy-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_12_zacks_rank_upgrade-3023272","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793808003.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Should Value Investors Buy RPC (RES) Stock?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3022928/should-value-investors-buy-rpc-res-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_2